---
import '../styles.css';
import { Matchup, OddsTable, SwingBoard } from '../components/islands';
import { readFileSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';

const has = existsSync(new URL('../../public/data.json', import.meta.url));
const data = has ? JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL('../../public/data.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8')) : null;
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>VALOPS Champions Shanghai 2026 predictor</title>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Champions Shanghai</h1>
    {data && <p class="favline"><strong>{data.teams[0].name}</strong> {(data.teams[0].title * 100).toFixed(1)}% to win</p>}
    <p class="dateline">Sep 24 to Oct 18 · 16 teams</p>
  </header>

  {data && (<>
  <section>
    <h2>Title odds</h2>
    <OddsTable teams={data.teams} client:load />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Matchup</h2>
    <Matchup teams={data.teams} matchups={data.matchups} client:load />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Groups</h2>
    <p class="sub">Opener win odds, then advance odds.</p>
    {Object.entries(data.bracket).map(([g, b]) => (
      <div class="team">
        <div class="teamhead"><span>Group {g}</span></div>
        {b.openers.map(o => (
          <div class="prow"><span>{data.teams.find(t => t.id === o.a)?.name} vs {data.teams.find(t => t.id === o.b)?.name}</span>
          <div class="bar"><i style={{ width: `${o.p * 100}%` }} /></div>
          <span class="num">{(o.p * 100).toFixed(0)}</span></div>
        ))}
        <table>
          <tbody>
            {b.odds.sort((x, y) => y.adv - x.adv).map(o => (
              <tr><td>{o.name}</td>
              <td class="num">{(o.adv * 100).toFixed(1)}</td>
              <td class="detail">2-0 {(o.first * 100).toFixed(0)} · 2-1 {(o.second * 100).toFixed(0)}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Teams</h2>
    {data.teams.map(t => (
      <div class="team">
        <div class="teamhead"><span>{t.name}</span>
        <span class="num mut">avg {t.roster.length ? Math.round(t.roster.reduce((s, p) => s + p.elo, 0) / t.roster.length) : '–'}</span></div>
        {t.roster.map(p => (
          <div class="prow"><span>{p.name}</span>
          <div class="bar"><i style={{ width: `${Math.max(4, Math.min(100, (p.elo - 1400) / 4))}%` }} /></div>
          <span class="num mut">{Math.round(p.elo)}</span></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th>
        <th title="Attack round win %">atk</th>
        <th title="Defense round win %">def</th>
        <th title="Pistol round win %">pistol</th>
        <th title="First-half round win %">1st</th>
        <th title="Second-half round win %">2nd</th>
        <th title="Share of rounds played in overtime">OT</th>
        <th title="Maps won after trailing by 4+ rounds">comeback</th>
        <th title="Maps lost after leading by 4+ rounds">choke</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {(() => {
          const rows = data.dna;
          const keys = ['atk','dfn','pistol','h1','h2','ot','comeback','choke'];
          const lo = {}, hi = {};
          keys.forEach(k => { lo[k] = Math.min(...rows.map(r => r[k])); hi[k] = Math.max(...rows.map(r => r[k])); });
          return rows.map(r => (
            <tr><td>{r.name}</td>{keys.map(k => (
              (r[k] === hi[k] || r[k] === lo[k])
                ? <td class="num"><strong>{r[k].toFixed(1)}</strong></td>
                : <td class="num">{r[k].toFixed(1)}</td>
            ))}</tr>
          ));
        })()}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2026 Swing leaders</h2>
    <p class="sub">Impact per 100 rounds.</p>
    <SwingBoard rows={data.swing} client:load />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Experts vs model</h2>
    <p class="sub">Nine Plat Chat lists merged into one Top 40. Ours is SWING-AR rank among Champions players only.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Player</th><th>Ours</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {(() => {
          const champs = data.swing.filter(p => p.champs);
          const rank = Object.fromEntries(champs.map((p, i) => [p.name.toLowerCase(), i + 1]));
          const board = ['Asuna','N4RRATE','something','brawk','lukxo','erde','Dambi','Francis','PatMen','slowly','nAts','xavi8k','Sayonara','s0pp','Meteor','kamo','trent','Cryocells','UdoTan','Timotino','dos9','keiko','BuZz','jawgemo','ZmjjKK','bang','Chronicle','WsLeo','GSR','Erv','Autumn','f0rsakeN','d4v41','Jinggg','Avez','SiuFatBB','NoMan','mada','invy','splash'];
          return board.map((name, i) => (
            <tr><td class="num">{i + 1}</td><td>{name}</td>
            <td class="num">{rank[name.toLowerCase()] ?? '–'}</td></tr>
          ));
        })()}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="method">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>The data</span></div>
      <p>Every pro series, map by map and round by round: scores, kills, agents, economy. It lands in one database of teams, players, and maps, and every feature below is computed from history before match day. Nothing peeks at the future.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>Player Elo</span></div>
      <div class="formula">R&#8242; = R + K(S &#8722; E)</div>
      <div class="formula">E = 1 / (1 + 10<sup>(R<sub>b</sub> &#8722; R<sub>a</sub>)/400</sup>)</div>
      <p>Ratings live on players, not teams, so they survive roster moves. Beating a stronger team moves a rating more, and big stages move ratings more than group games. Every offseason, ratings drift 30% back toward average.</p>
      <p>A team's rating is the mean of its five players, minus a penalty for a new lineup. Two trackers run side by side: a slow one for true strength and a fast one that reacts 1.5x to every result and never regresses. The gap between them reads as form.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>The features</span></div>
      <p>Each matchup becomes a list of A-minus-B gaps: rating, recent form, last-60-day stats (rating, ACS, KAST, first-kill differential), series win rate, strength of schedule, days of rest, agent-composition coverage, pistol and retake rates. Small samples get smoothed toward average, so a three-map hot streak cannot break the math.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>Win probability</span></div>
      <div class="formula">P(A beats B) = 1 / (1 + e<sup>&#8722;w&#183;x</sup>)</div>
      <p>A plain logistic regression turns the gaps into a probability. The weights are readable and the rating gaps carry the most weight.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>Evaluation</span></div>
      <p>We train on past years and test on the next one. Lower Brier is better.</p>
      <div class="brier">
        {data.validation.filter(v => v.test).map((v) => (
          <div class="brow"><span class="blabel">{v.test} model</span><div class="btrack"><i style={`width: ${(v.brier / 0.3 * 100).toFixed(1)}%`}></i></div><span class="num">{v.brier.toFixed(3)}</span></div>
          <div class="brow dim"><span class="blabel">{v.test} coinflip</span><div class="btrack"><i style="width: 83.3%"></i></div><span class="num">0.250</span></div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>At the extremes the model is overconfident: matchups priced at 77% win 62% of the time.</p>
      <p>A change ships only if walk-forward Brier improves.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>Simulation</span></div>
      <p>We run 10,000 sims over the real groups and bracket.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="teamhead"><span>Player scores</span></div>
      <div class="formula">swing(round) = P(win | score + 1) &#8722; P(win | score)</div>
      <p>Every round is worth its win-probability jump. An 11-11 round moves the needle far more than a 12-3 round, so clutch rounds pay more. A map's total swing is split across the winning five by kills, first kills, assists, and survival, weighted by role.</p>
      <div class="formula">Space = (first kills + first deaths) / rounds</div>
      <p>Space is engagement rate: how often a player takes the first duel of a round.</p>
      <div class="formula">SWING-AR = (swing &#8722; replacement swing) / rounds &#215; 100</div>
      <p>Replacement level is the 20th percentile of the player's role, so a duelist is judged against duelists. Swing is opponent-adjusted first: credit scales as 1 + (opponent Elo &#8722; 1500) / 400, so beating an elite team pays more than farming a weak region.</p>
    </div>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Split</th><th>Brier</th><th>Acc</th><th>n</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {data.validation.filter(v => v.test).map((v) => (
          <tr><td class="num">thru {v.train_thru} → {v.test}</td>
          <td class="num">{v.brier}</td><td class="num">{v.acc}</td><td class="num">{v.n_test}</td></tr>
        ))}
        <tr><td class="num">coinflip</td>
        <td class="num">{data.validation.find(v => v.baseline_coinflip_brier)?.baseline_coinflip_brier}</td><td class="num">–</td><td class="num">–</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  </>)}
</div>
</body>
</html>
